  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so there is no evidence yet about which design choices matter. The most informative first experiment is to establish the simplest possible baseline: RNA-only, single-profile, PCA-2000 representation. This configuration serves as the null reference against which every other design decision (multiprofile aggregation, learned encoders like scVI/scGPT, image modality, and fusion strategies) can be measured. Without this floor, we cannot determine whether added complexity (multiprofile, transformer aggregation, multimodal fusion) actually improves validation accuracy or merely adds variance. Config_001 is the cleanest single-modality, single-profile, linear-representation baseline, isolating the fundamental signal in the RNA data before any architectural complexity is introduced. It is the highest-information-per-experiment choice under a limited budget because it anchors the entire search space."
